    {
      "id": "fi5m3nrzhyQQG0G21kx0h",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -11070.679080239317,
      "y": 34183.800453353164,
      "width": 1402.8192138671875,
      "height": 775,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "a8",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1702746638,
      "version": 1416,
      "versionNonce": 1279605906,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1783146138981,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Sharing the file\n1. Poor Approach : add a share list to file metadata\n    - add a list of users who have access to the file directly to file metadata\n    {\n      \"id\": \"123\",\n      \"name\": \"file.txt\",\n      \"size\": 1000,\n      \"mimeType\": \"text/plain\",\n      \"uploadedBy\": \"user1\",\n      \"sharelist\": [\"user2\", \"user3\"]\n    }\n    - When on our website user expect to see all the files they own and shared to them on the dashboard\n        - All files they own is fast enough - query using an index on uploadedBy\n        - Getting list of files shared with them is slow, need to scan sharelist of every file to see if the user is in there\n2. Good Solution : caching to speed up fetching the sharelist\n    - mapping of list of all the files shared to the current user from all other users\n    user1:[\"fileId1\", \"fileId2\"]\n    - This way we know the list of files shared with the current user by checking our sharedFiles cache.\n    - Problem is sharedFiles cache need to be in sync with sharelist of filemetadata\n    - To overcome this keep sharelist and sharedFiles in the same DB and update both list in a single txn.\n3. Great Solution : create a separate table for shares\n    SharedFiles Table\n    | userId (Partition Key) | fileId (Sort Key) |\n    |-------------|-------------|\n    | user1       | fileId1     |\n    | user1       | fileId2     |\n    | user2       | fileId3     |\n    \n    - userId and fileId together form a composite primary key, allowing the same user to have multiple files shared with them.\n    - slightly less efficient than previous approach as need to query a table now but the tradeoff is worth it as no need to sync two lists now.\n",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Sharing the file\n1. Poor Approach : add a share list to file metadata\n    - add a list of users who have access to the file directly to file metadata\n    {\n      \"id\": \"123\",\n      \"name\": \"file.txt\",\n      \"size\": 1000,\n      \"mimeType\": \"text/plain\",\n      \"uploadedBy\": \"user1\",\n      \"sharelist\": [\"user2\", \"user3\"]\n    }\n    - When on our website user expect to see all the files they own and shared to them on the dashboard\n        - All files they own is fast enough - query using an index on uploadedBy\n        - Getting list of files shared with them is slow, need to scan sharelist of every file to see if the user is in there\n2. Good Solution : caching to speed up fetching the sharelist\n    - mapping of list of all the files shared to the current user from all other users\n    user1:[\"fileId1\", \"fileId2\"]\n    - This way we know the list of files shared with the current user by checking our sharedFiles cache.\n    - Problem is sharedFiles cache need to be in sync with sharelist of filemetadata\n    - To overcome this keep sharelist and sharedFiles in the same DB and update both list in a single txn.\n3. Great Solution : create a separate table for shares\n    SharedFiles Table\n    | userId (Partition Key) | fileId (Sort Key) |\n    |-------------|-------------|\n    | user1       | fileId1     |\n    | user1       | fileId2     |\n    | user2       | fileId3     |\n    \n    - userId and fileId together form a composite primary key, allowing the same user to have multiple files shared with them.\n    - slightly less efficient than previous approach as need to query a table now but the tradeoff is worth it as no need to sync two lists now.\n",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "-WgExtmQ2ivkfvw4DaPL3",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -11034.427532857206,
      "y": 35003.17807278445,
      "width": 1209.419189453125,
      "height": 700,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
